<title>UK: Baltic Republics fund raises $21 million.</title>
<headline>Baltic Republics fund raises $21 million.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Republics Fund has raised $21 million via an issue of conversion, or C, shares, against an original target of $20 million, manager Societe Generale Emerging European Markets said.</p>
<p>&quot;The fund will take advantage of opportunities in Latvia and Lithuania,&quot; SGEEM director Patrick Shanahan told Reuters.</p>
<p>The fund which had $40 million and is listed in Dublin, is one of the best performers this year.</p>
<p>&quot;Some companies in the region are looking at capital increases to expand their businesses,&quot; Shanahan said. The C shares will convert once the proceeds of the issue are 90 percent invested, which will probably occur in 12-18 months after the issue, SGEEM said.</p>
<p>-- David Chance London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
